            <ArticleTitle>Childhood back pain: diagnostic evaluation of an unusual case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>334-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Low back pain is uncommon in children. The case of a 5-year-old boy presenting with back pain that proved to be caused by a metastatic primitive neuroectodermal tumor is presented and the evaluation of such patients is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
